## How to review

Use `gh` for everything; you do NOT need to clone the repo.

1. Read the diff: `gh pr diff {{ issue.identifier }}` (or split by file with
   `gh pr diff {{ issue.identifier }} --name-only` and then `gh api`).
2. Check CI status: `gh pr checks {{ issue.identifier }}`. Mention failing
   checks if relevant, but don't block on them — review the code anyway.
3. Look at prior review context if needed:
   `gh pr view {{ issue.identifier }} --json reviews,comments`.

## Filing the review

Submit ONE batched review with all inline comments + verdict in a single
API call. Do NOT loop `POST /pulls/<num>/comments` per line — each call
creates its own COMMENTED review entry and spams the PR's reviews list.

    REPO="$(echo '{{ issue.identifier }}' | awk -F# '{print $1}')"
    PR_NUM="$(echo '{{ issue.identifier }}' | awk -F# '{print $2}')"
    gh api "repos/$REPO/pulls/$PR_NUM/reviews" \
      --method POST \
      --field event=APPROVE \
      --field body='<summary>' \
      --raw-field comments='[
        {"path":"foo.py","line":42,"side":"RIGHT","body":"..."}
      ]'

`event` values: `APPROVE` (LGTM), `REQUEST_CHANGES` (must-fix),
`COMMENT` (FYI / nits / questions, or you can't fully review yet).

Verify the review landed:

    gh api "repos/$REPO/pulls/$PR_NUM/reviews" \
      --jq '.[-1] | {user: .user.login, state, body}'

Avoid `gh pr review` — it exits 0 with empty stdout on success, which
will trick you into retrying and double-approving the PR. Stick with
`gh api` so the response body confirms success.

## Done signal

Submitting any review records you in the PR's `reviews` list, which is
symphony's "you're done" signal — no labels to remove. Works for both
individually-requested and team-requested PRs (team requests don't auto-
clear, but your own review record does). If you genuinely can't review
the PR (e.g. need more context from the author), leave a `--comment`
review saying so; that still satisfies the gate.
